<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48943" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θόλος</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>round building with conical roof,
				rotunda</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				22.442
			</span></i>, al., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> at Athens, <i>the
			Rotunda</i>, in which the Prytaneis, etc., dined, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ap.</u>
				32c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.45
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				19.249
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				43.3
			</span></i>, Alexand. Com.<i><span class="en">
				9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				1.5.1
			</span></i>; a similar building at Epidaurus, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.27.3
			</span></i>; at Magnesia on Maeander, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				589.43
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θόλος, ὁ</span>,
			in public baths, <i>vaulted vapour-bath,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PMagd.
				33.3
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Asclep.Myrl.
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				11.501d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				1.23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				2145.6
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMag.Osl.</u>
				1
			</span></i>. <i><span class="en">
				75
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>bandage</i> for the head, invented by Diocles, <i><span class="en">
				Heliod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				48.25
			</span></i> tit.</div>
